{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiremachost"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"HeadwireMacHost","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"HeadwireMacHost","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireMacHost"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Headwire Helper’s streaming, input and pairing: the code that serves paired devices from the Mac.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"HeadwireMacHost runs the helper’s host. It listens for paired devices on the USB cable, the network and Direct wireless over TLS with both keys pinned, captures a display with ScreenCaptureKit, encodes it with a low-latency HEVC encoder, sends the frames and the Mac’s sound to each device, and posts the input each device sends back as "},{"code":"CGEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s. It also runs the pairing window, keeps the trust list and the helper’s key in the keychain, draws the calibration strip a device asks for, and reads the iPad’s source mode request over the Bluetooth link the Mac already holds for HID. It does not decide what a person sees: the menu’s switches, the permissions, the build and the capture display’s mode are resolved by "},{"code":"HeadwireMacKit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s value types, and the menu itself belongs to the "},{"code":"HeadwireMac","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" app. The wire formats come from "},{"code":"HeadwireWire","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the input events from "},{"code":"HeadwireInput","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so both ends share one implementation. Much of the streaming and input code is derived from "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Saffsanity\/sill","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", under the Apache License 2.0."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The virtual display, Sidecar and the private Bluetooth pairing agent are compiled only into the Direct build and are not documented here."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/SessionLifecycle"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCoordinator","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostConfiguration","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/SessionInfo","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/StreamHealth","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostCounters","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostLog"],"anchor":"Running-the-host","title":"Running the host"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/PairingService","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/TrustList","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/PairedDevice","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostKeys","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/LinkAddresses"],"anchor":"Pairing-and-trust","title":"Pairing and trust"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostInputActor","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/InputDeviceID","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/InputInjector","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/EventPoster","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/LiveEventPoster","doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/DryRunEventPoster"],"anchor":"Input","title":"Input"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHos